# Rollback point for the PAT-1 window-registration change

PURPOSE
    This file records the last commit before a breaking change, and the
    exact steps to undo that change. Delete this file once the change
    has held in production for a release.

LAST GOOD COMMIT
    d159255  docs(debt-ts-1): do not nudge the apps team
    2026-10-21, CI green, tree clean.

WHAT CHANGES AFTER THIS POINT
    64 component classes stop being registered on `window`. Before the
    change a consumer could write `new window.SizesPicker(options)` and
    receive an object whose 14 private fields are ordinary properties,
    because TypeScript removes the `private` keyword at compile time.
    After the change the only way in is the factory, for example
    `window.createSizesPicker(options)`.

    Every `window.create*` factory is UNCHANGED. Nothing that calls a
    factory is affected. Only direct construction breaks.

    Measured before the change: the knobby application does not
    construct these classes, and `component-library.d.ts` declares none
    of them. Six demo pages in this repository did, and they were
    changed to use their factories. The remaining risk is a consumer
    nobody has counted.

HOW TO ROLL BACK

    1. Find the commit that made the change. It is the first commit
       after d159255 whose subject begins `fix(pat-1)!:`.

           git log --oneline d159255..HEAD

    2. Revert it. This restores the 64 registrations and leaves every
       later commit in place, which is the safe option on a shared
       branch.

           git revert --no-edit <that commit>
           npm run build
           npm test
           git push

    3. If several commits are involved, revert the range newest first.

           git revert --no-edit <oldest>^..<newest>

    4. Only if the branch is not shared and you want the tree exactly
       as it was:

           git reset --hard d159255

       This discards every commit after d159255, including this file.
       Prefer step 2.

HOW TO TELL WHETHER THE ROLLBACK WORKED
    Load any component bundle and check for the class global:

        node -e 'global.window={};
          new Function(require("fs").readFileSync(
            "dist/components/sizespicker/sizespicker.js","utf8"))();
          console.log(Object.keys(window));'

    Before the change and after a rollback, the output contains both
    `SizesPicker` and `createSizesPicker`. After the change it contains
    only `createSizesPicker`.

WHO TO TELL
    The apps team consumes this library from static.knobby.io. They are
    mid-way through a large piece of work (see DEBT-TS-1), so tell them
    rather than asking them to act.
